      "content": "Start by immediately pausing the refund and requesting clear, high-resolution photos of the damage along with the packing slip to verify the shipment details. If the packaging was unsealed or labeled as customer-opened, politely decline the full refund and offer a store credit or a replacement instead, which often satisfies customers while protecting your margins. Finally, document this interaction thoroughly to set a consistent precedent that prevents future abuse without escalating into a costly dispute.",
