    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "Got it. I'm looking at the carrier sensor logs for this specific tracking number right now, and honestly, everything shows the package was handled perfectly and the vibrations/impact sensors stayed well within safe limits during transit. The data suggests the damage didn't happen during shipping. \n\nIf the logs show no issues, should we be even stricter with the refund? I don't want to waste company money if it's clearly a customer issue, but I also don't want a PR headache. What's your take given what the sensor data is telling us?",
